{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 104,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bless the LORD, O my soul. O LORD my God, thou art very great; thou art clothed with honor and majesty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who coverest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thyself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with light as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a garment: who stretchest out the heavens like a curtain:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who layeth the beams of his chambers in the waters: who maketh the clouds his chariot: who walketh upon the wings of the wind:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who maketh his angels spirits; his ministers a flaming fire:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " laid the foundations of the earth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it should not be removed for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou coveredst it with the deep as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a garment: the waters stood above the mountains.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At thy rebuke they fled; at the voice of thy thunder they hasted away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They go up by the mountains; they go down by the valleys to the place which thou hast founded for them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast set a bound that they may not pass over; that they turn not again to cover the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He sendeth the springs into the valleys, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " run among the hills.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They give drink to every beast of the field: the wild asses quench their thirst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "By them shall the fowls of the heaven have their habitation, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " sing among the branches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He watereth the hills from his chambers: the earth is satisfied with the fruit of thy works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He causeth the grass to grow for the cattle, and herb for the service of man: that he may bring forth food out of the earth;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And wine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " maketh glad the heart of man, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " oil to make ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " face to shine, and bread ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " strengtheneth man's heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The trees of the LORD are full ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of sap",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; the cedars of Lebanon, which he hath planted;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Where the birds make their nests: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the stork, the fir-trees ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " her house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The high hills ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a refuge for the wild goats; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the rocks for the conies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He appointeth the moon for seasons: the sun knoweth his going down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest darkness, and it is night: in which all the beasts of the forest do creep ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "forth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The young lions roar after their prey, and seek their food from God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sun ariseth, they collect, and lay themselves down in their dens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Man goeth forth to his work and to his labor until the evening.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O LORD, how manifold are thy works! in wisdom hast thou made them all: the earth is full of thy riches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " this great and wide sea, in which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " creeping animals innumerable, both small and great beasts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There go the ships: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that leviathan, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou hast made to play therein.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These wait all upon thee; that thou mayest give ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their food in due season.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou givest them, they gather: thou openest thy hand, they are filled with good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hidest thy face, they are troubled: thou takest away their breath, they die, and return to their dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou sendest forth thy spirit, they are created: and thou renewest the face of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The glory of the LORD shall endure for ever: the LORD shall rejoice in his works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He looketh on the earth, and it trembleth: he toucheth the hills, and they smoke.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will sing to the LORD as long as I live: I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My meditation of him shall be sweet: I will be glad in the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.104.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let sinners be consumed out of the earth, and let the wicked be no more. Bless thou the LORD, O my soul. Praise ye the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
